KJÆR & DALGAARD ADVOKATPARTNERSELSKAB

Skolegade 12, 8000 Aarhus C, Denmark — CVR 3817 5524 — our ref. KD/SBC/2024-117

BY COURIER AND E-MAIL (legal@korvane.example)

Korvane Cold Chain Sp. z o.o., ul. Łużycka 14, 81-537 Gdynia, Poland
For the attention of Ms Marta Kowarzik, Chief Executive Officer, and Ms Sofia Brandão, Legal Counsel
Copy to Mr Yusuf Demirkıran, Key Account Manager

Aarhus, 2 September 2024

**NOTICE OF TERMINATION — Seasonal Cold Chain Services Agreement of 18 March 2021 between Korvane Cold Chain Sp. z o.o. and Samsø Berry Co-op amba (your ref. KCC/SBC/2021/011)**

Dear Ms Kowarzik, dear Ms Brandão,

We act for Samsø Berry Co-op amba ("the Co-op"), registered office Havnevej 9, 8305 Samsø, Denmark. We write on the Co-op's instructions, following its board meeting of 27 August 2024, to give you notice of termination of the above Agreement, and to set out how the Co-op expects the exit to be handled.

**1. Termination**

Under clause 14.3 of the Agreement the Co-op may terminate for cause on 60 days' written notice if Korvane fails to collect within the agreed Pick-up Window in three or more instances during one calendar month. The Pick-up Window is the 2-hour slot fixed for each collection at the Co-op's packing shed at Ballen harbour. In June 2024, which as you know is the busiest month of the strawberry season, Korvane missed the Pick-up Window on 4 June (by 4 hours 20 minutes), on 11 June (by 7 hours) and on 21 June (by a full day, the load being collected on 22 June). The consequence for the Co-op's members was that three consignments of strawberries, which should have gone on the evening ferry, were collected after the berries had already been held at ambient temperature on the quay, as recorded by the Co-op's own data loggers, and were downgraded by the buyer at Hamburg.

The Co-op therefore terminates the Agreement under clause 14.3, with effect from 1 November 2024 (the "Termination Date"), being 60 days after the date of this letter. Korvane's colleague Mr Demirkıran wrote by e-mail on 28 June 2024 that Korvane "will make this right" and that the June performance was caused by a shortage of drivers; the Co-op took that as acknowledgement of the facts but the promised improvement did not materialise in July, when two further windows were missed (2 July and 16 July).

**2. Loss claimed**

The members of the Co-op suffered a loss on the downgraded consignments, which we put at DKK 486,000, being the difference between the price of Class I and Class II berries on the Hamburg market on the dates concerned, plus the cost of re-packing. The Co-op will claim that sum from Korvane. We ask you to respond to the claim in writing within 21 days of the date of this letter, that is by 23 September 2024. We note that clause 11.2 of the Agreement caps Korvane's liability for each season at 1.5 times the freight fees invoiced for that season, and the Co-op's claim lies within that limit on any view.

**3. Return of equipment and deposit**

During the term the Co-op has held 180 KC-Tag 4 loggers supplied by Korvane against a deposit. The Co-op will return all 180 loggers, cleaned and with their batteries as found, within 14 days after the Termination Date, to Korvane's depot at Hamburg-Waltershof, at Korvane's cost for the carriage. Korvane shall refund the deposit of DKK 212,400, being DKK 1,180 per logger, within 30 days after the Termination Date, subject only to deduction for any logger not returned, at the same rate of DKK 1,180 each.

**4. Final account**

The Co-op asks for a final statement of account within 30 days after the Termination Date. The Co-op's own calculation of the items it expects to see is as follows.

| Item | Amount (DKK) |
|---|---|
| Season freight invoiced by Korvane, 2024 to date | 2,140,000 |
| Season rebate under clause 8.4 (3.2% of freight) | 68,480 |
| Logger deposit | 212,400 |
| Credit note promised for the 2 July collection failure | 38,750 |

The rebate in clause 8.4 is payable on the freight invoiced for the season up to the Termination Date and the Co-op does not accept that the termination alters this.

**5. Preservation and governing law**

The Co-op asks Korvane to preserve all documents, data and recordings relating to its collections in June and July 2024, including dispatch records, driver logs and tracking data, and the Tidewalk alert history for its consignments. The Agreement is governed by Danish law and clause 19 gives the Maritime and Commercial Court in Copenhagen (Sø- og Handelsretten) exclusive jurisdiction. The Co-op reserves all its rights, including as to the claim in section 2, and nothing in this letter waives any of them.

Please confirm receipt of this notice, and the points in sections 3 and 4, by 16 September 2024. We would prefer to agree the practical exit with you without proceedings, and Mr Dalgaard is available for a call on any weekday between 09:00 and 15:00 Danish time.

Yours faithfully,

Mette Dalgaard, partner
Kjær & Dalgaard Advokatpartnerselskab
Direct: +45 5550 0172 — md@kjaer-dalgaard.example

(Handwritten at the foot of the Korvane file copy, S.B., 4 September: "Rebate maths is right. 3.2% of 2,140,000. Credit note NOT promised in writing by us — check with Yusuf. Hold notice to be extended to cover SBC, ask Kamil.")
